  "question": "Evaluate $\\frac{d}{dx}\\left[\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{2x}{1-x^2}\\right)\\right]$ and hence deduce the derivative of $\\tan^{-1}(\\tan 2x)$ w.r.t. $x$ for $|x| < \\frac{\\pi}{4}$.",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "$\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{2x}{1-x^2}\\right) = 2\\tan^{-1}(x)$ for $|x| < 1$.<br /><br />Differentiating: $\\frac{d}{dx}(2\\tan^{-1}x) = 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{1 + x^2}$.<br /><br />For $|x| < \\frac{\\pi}{4}$, $\\tan^{-1}(\\tan 2x) = 2x$.<br /><br />Hence, derivative is $2$.",
  "explanation_image": [],
