    "A": "$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{2x}{1-x^2}\\right)\\right]=\\dfrac{1}{1+x^2}$<br />and $\\dfrac{d}{dx}[\\tan^{-1}(\\tan2x)]=1$",
    "B": "$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{2x}{1-x^2}\\right)\\right]=\\dfrac{2}{1-x^2}$<br />and $\\dfrac{d}{dx}[\\tan^{-1}(\\tan2x)]=2$",
    "C": "$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{2x}{1-x^2}\\right)\\right]=\\dfrac{2}{1+x^2}$<br />and $\\dfrac{d}{dx}[\\tan^{-1}(\\tan2x)]=2$",
    "D": "$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{2x}{1-x^2}\\right)\\right]=2$<br />and $\\dfrac{d}{dx}[\\tan^{-1}(\\tan2x)]=\\dfrac{2}{1+x^2}$"
